# SDK Technical Extraction Skill

Skill chuyên biệt để trích xuất thông tin kỹ thuật SDK từ các trang documentation.

## Khi nào sử dụng

- Khi user cần lấy SDK requirements cho integration
- Khi cần extract installation/configuration instructions
- Khi cần trích xuất API methods và type definitions
- Khi cần thu thập code examples cho implementation

## Target Content Types

### 1. Installation & Setup
- Package manager commands (npm, yarn, pnpm, pip, go, etc.)
- Peer/optional dependencies
- System requirements
- Environment setup

### 2. Configuration
- Environment variables
- Configuration files
- Initialization options
- Plugin registrations

### 3. Authentication
- API keys setup
- OAuth flows
- Token management
- Permission scopes

### 4. API Methods
- Class/function signatures
- Parameters và types
- Return values
- Error handling

### 5. Type Definitions
- Interfaces/classes
- Enums/constants
- Generic types
- Union types

### 6. Code Examples
- Basic usage
- Advanced patterns
- Error handling
- Best practices

## Extraction Workflow

### Phase 1: Initial Survey

```bash
# Mở SDK documentation page
"$PWCLI" open https://docs.sdk-vendor.com/sdk/latest

# Lấy overview
"$PWCLI" snapshot
"$PWCLI" eval "document.title"
"$PWCLI" eval "document.querySelector('meta[name=description]')?.content"

# Lấy table of contents/navigation
"$PWCLI" eval "JSON.stringify(Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('nav a, [class*=sidebar] a')).map(a => ({text: a.textContent.trim(), href: a.getAttribute('href')}))"
```

### Phase 2: Installation Section

```bash
# Navigate to Installation section
"$PWCLI" click e5  # Element ref cho Installation nav
"$PWCLI" snapshot

# Extract package install commands
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre code')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/(npm install|yarn add|pip install|go get)/)).map(el => el.textContent)"

# Extract peer dependencies
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('tr, li')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/peer|depend/i)).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### Phase 3: Configuration Section

```bash
# Navigate to Configuration
"$PWCLI" click e7
"$PWCLI" snapshot

# Extract env variables
"$PWCLI" eval "JSON.stringify(Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=env], [id*=env], table tr')).map(tr => ({name: tr.children[0]?.textContent, desc: tr.children[1]?.textContent, required: tr.children[2]?.textContent})))"

# Extract config options
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre code')).map(c => c.textContent)"
```

### Phase 4: Authentication Section

```bash
# Navigate to Auth section
"$PWCLI" click e9
"$PWCLI" snapshot

# Extract auth setup code
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre')).map(p => p.textContent)"

# Extract auth parameters
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=param], [class*=option]')).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

### Phase 5: API Reference

```bash
# Navigate to API Reference
"$PWCLI" click e11
"$PWCLI" snapshot

# Extract method signatures
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=signature], [class*=method], pre')).map(el => el.textContent)"

# Extract parameter tables
"$PWCLI" eval "JSON.stringify(Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('table')).map(t => ({headers: Array.from(t.querySelectorAll('th')).map(h => h.textContent), rows: Array.from(t.querySelectorAll('tbody tr')).map(r => Array.from(r.children).map(c => c.textContent))})))"
```

### Phase 6: Type Definitions

```bash
# Navigate to Types section
"$PWCLI" click e13
"$PWCLI" snapshot

# Extract type definitions (TypeScript/Flow)
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('pre code')).filter(el => el.textContent.match(/^(interface|type|class|enum)/)).map(el => el.textContent)"

# Extract examples
"$PWCLI" eval "Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('[class*=example]')).map(el => el.textContent)"
```

